					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13965182</guid>
				<title>SCP-5870</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13965182/scp-5870</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 30 Dec 2020 11:24:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Veralta</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6030962</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hello! Veralta's here with a new SCP about koalas, nature, the future of Australia, and intricate worldbuilding based on the beliefs of aboriginal Australian people like the Bundjalung and the Eora. Consider this SCP a free New Year trip through Australia, and a little bit of a crash course on the Australian condition.</p> <p>Also, it's linked to Ralliston's Obearwatch Command; fun fact, all of these started when he threw the word &quot;Koalalition&quot; at me, and I said, &quot;Hmm&#8230; uwah, this looks interesting&quot;. I initially planned out a short article with a gimmick and a punchline.</p> <p>But then, I realized I had to dive deep into the waterhole.</p> <p>The aboriginal Australian belief system, also called Dreamtime<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-482354-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, is very complex and interesting. It would be a shame if I just went with a silly punchline when aboriginal culture, with its mix of hopes and dreams for Australia, needs a chance to shine here.</p> <p>Lastly, consider this article as a piece dedicated to Australians and wildlife - such as the koalas themselves - who have been affected by the severe bushfires. As a Filipino youth, I couldn't do much to be honest, aside from raising awareness. I tried to stay true to the myths' essence while adding my style of writing to them, while I researched news about the bushfires.</p> <p>All in all, though, please enjoy this SCP, and I wish a Happy New Year - and more happy years - to come for all of us!</p> <p>Special thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ralliston" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5986843&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="Ralliston" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5986843)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ralliston" >Ralliston</a></span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-482354-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/meisteroni" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6750228&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="Meisteroni" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6750228)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/meisteroni" >Meisteroni</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drchandra" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1956625&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="DrChandra" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1956625)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drchandra" >DrChandra</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rose-the-changeling" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4701019&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="Rose the Changeling " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4701019)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rose-the-changeling" >Rose the Changeling</a></span> , for concept checking and making my narrative is solid. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dysadron" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4384469&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="Dysadron" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4384469)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dysadron" >Dysadron</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/caspian2" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5343993&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="caspian2" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5343993)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/caspian2" >caspian2</a></span> also have my gratitude for their comprehensively good LBL and critique. Last but not the least, I also want to give a well-deserved shoutout to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-balthazaar" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1468535&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609341352" alt="Dr Balthazaar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1468535)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-balthazaar" >Dr Balthazaar</a></span> for providing guidance on Australian beliefs and culture. You guys are amazing!</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-482354-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. By the way, this word does not cover what the beliefs really mean, and while dreaming is a part of the culture, it is not just that. Additionally, the word &quot;Dreamtime&quot; may even be just a mistranslation of words meant for deities.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-482354-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. Bear goes rawr :p</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
